/* book: lead: A rolling bearing fails by fatigue, not at one fixed load. Heavy load shortens life. Makers give two numbers: C, the basic dynamic load rating, and C₀, the basic static load rating. From C and the equivalent load P you get L₁₀, the life reached by 90 of 100 identical bearings. This chapter computes L₁₀ = (C/P)p in million revolutions, then in hours, and handles a load that changes through the day. */
