/* book Worked example: Q: A deep-groove ball bearing on a pump shaft has C = 30 kN. The shaft runs at n = 1500 rpm. The equivalent dynamic load is P = 6 kN. Find L10 in million revolutions and in hours.
   1. Check units: C = 30 kN and P = 6 kN are both in kN, so C/P is a pure number.
   2. Ball bearing: p = 3.
   3. C/P = 30/6 = 5.
   4. L10 = 5³ = 125 million revolutions.
   5. Revolutions per hour: 60 × 1500 = 90 000.
   6. L10h = 125 × 10⁶ ÷ 90 000 = 1388.9 hours.
   Answer: L10 = 125 million revolutions, which at 1500 rpm is L10h ≈ 1389 hours. */
