/* book Worked example 2: Q: The same bearing (C = 30 kN) on a conveyor runs 50 % of the time at 3 kN and 1500 rpm, 30 % at 5 kN and 1000 rpm, and 20 % at 8 kN and 500 rpm. Find the mean equivalent load, L10 and the life in hours.
   1. Weights ni ti: 1500 × 0.5 = 750, 1000 × 0.3 = 300, 500 × 0.2 = 100. Their sum, the mean speed, is 1150 rpm.
   2. Load terms Pi³ ni ti (P in kN): 27 × 750 = 20 250; 125 × 300 = 37 500; 512 × 100 = 51 200. Sum = 108 950.
   3. Pe³ = 108 950/1150 = 94.74, so Pe = 94.741/3 = 4.559 kN.
   4. L10 = (30/4.559)³ = 6.581³ = 285.0 million revolutions.
   5. L10h = 285.0 × 10⁶ ÷ (60 × 1150) = 4130 hours.
   6. Notice that the 8 kN step, only a fifth of the time and at the lowest speed, gives nearly half of the damage (51 200 of 108 950).
   Answer: Pe ≈ 4.56 kN, L10 ≈ 285 million revolutions and L10h ≈ 4130 hours. */
